---
description: Agent Reliability Lab conventions
alwaysApply: true
---

- Strict TypeScript. Do not use `any` without a comment explaining why.
- Keep files small and names clear. Do not leave dead code.
- Do not add dependencies that are not already in the project without asking.
- The LLM provider is Groq (`groq-sdk`, `GROQ_API_KEY`), not Anthropic. The public API reads `AGENT_MODEL` on the server and never accepts a model from the client.
- Keep the Groq client behind `src/core/llm.ts`. Tests use MockLLM. Tests and CI must not call the network.
- Every guard, trajectory matcher, and idempotency behaviour needs a unit test.
- Never fabricate evaluation results, percentages, or screenshots. Numbers in the UI and README come from `results/`. Leave gaps as `TODO(me)`.
- Never commit secrets. `.env*` stays gitignored except `.env.example`.
- Do not run paid evals unless the user explicitly asks. Eval scripts must print a cost ceiling and wait for `--yes`.
- Do not hard-code result numbers. If `results/` has no run, show an empty state.
- The agent loop is hand-written. Do not add LangGraph or the Vercel AI SDK agent helpers.
- Refund idempotency keys use the harness `requestId`, never a value from the model.
- A unique index on `refunds.idempotency_key` exists only when idempotent refunds are enabled.
